{"review":"draft","flags":[{"page":1,"note":"Scanned deck: all 95 pages were read from page images (OCR used only for search)."},{"page":26,"note":"The slide prints o₁ = (0.538, 0.532) and o₂ = (0.861, 0.793). With b_o = (0.1, 0.1) the outputs are (0.638, 0.533) and (0.960, 0.792): the first component omits the bias. The lesson uses the recomputed values."},{"page":36,"note":"BPTT forward pass: the t = 2 pre-activation's second entry should be 0.655 (0.076 + 0.079 + 0.5), not 0.576; h₂ and h₃ on the slide inherit the error. Recomputed values: h₂ = (0.500, 0.575), h₃ = (0.808, 0.774). The output gradient (−0.496, 0.496) and ∂L/∂h₃ = (−0.149, 0.149) agree to rounding."},{"page":57,"note":"Deep RNN t = 2: recomputed h₂⁽¹⁾ = (0.416, 0.488) and h₂⁽²⁾ = (0.443, 0.393); the slide shows (0.417, 0.451) and (0.408, 0.408). t = 1 values match."},{"page":64,"note":"The update-gate slide says 'z ≈ 0: keep old state; z ≈ 1: replace', which is the opposite of the deck's own eq. (34) h_t = z ⊙ h_{t−1} + (1 − z) ⊙ h̃_t and of slide 73. The lesson follows eq. (34) throughout."},{"page":93,"note":"Summary table gives the vanilla RNN count as 2h² + 2hd + 2h + Vh, inconsistent with p.23's h² + hd + h + Vh + V (used in the lesson and verified numerically)."},{"page":12,"note":"Eq. (6) writes P(x_t | x₁…x_{t−1}) = P(x_t | h_t) although h_t has already seen x_t; in the usual indexing the state h_{t−1} predicts x_t. The lesson notes this."}],"recall":{"defs":[["Hidden state h_t","Fixed-size summary of the sequence so far."],["Parameter sharing","Same weights at every time step."],["BPTT","Backprop on the unrolled graph, gradients summed over time."],["Vanishing gradient","Gradient shrinks exponentially with steps back."],["GRU","Reset + update gates; one state."],["LSTM","Forget, input, output gates + cell state."],["Bidirectional RNN","Forward and backward RNNs, states concatenated."],["Perplexity","exp(average per-token cross-entropy)."]],"formulas":["h_t=\\tanh(W_{hh}h_{t-1}+W_{hx}x_t+b_h)","o_t=W_{ho}h_t+b_o,\\ \\ P=\\mathrm{softmax}(o_t)","\\mathcal L=-\\sum_t\\log P(x_t\\mid x_{<t})","\\tfrac{\\partial\\mathcal L}{\\partial h_t}=\\tfrac{\\partial\\ell_t}{\\partial h_t}+\\tfrac{\\partial\\mathcal L}{\\partial h_{t+1}}\\mathrm{diag}(1-h_{t+1}^2)W_{hh}","h_t=z_t\\odot h_{t-1}+(1-z_t)\\odot\\tilde h_t","c_t=f_t\\odot c_{t-1}+i_t\\odot\\tilde c_t,\\ \\ h_t=o_t\\odot\\tanh(c_t)","\\text{params: } g\\,(hd+h^2+h)+Vh+V,\\ g=1,3,4"],"takeaways":["RNNs carry a hidden state through time with shared weights.","Train with BPTT; gradients sum over steps.","Plain RNNs suffer vanishing/exploding gradients.","GRU/LSTM gates give an additive path for memory and gradients.","Bidirectional needs the full sequence; stacked RNNs are usually 2–4 layers."],"confused":[["GRU update gate z","In this deck z ≈ 1 keeps the old state (eq. 34); some texts swap the convention."],["Cell state vs hidden state","c_t is long-term memory; h_t = o_t ⊙ tanh(c_t) is what is output."],["Bidirectional vs deep","Two directions at one level vs layers stacked on top."],["BPTT vs truncated BPTT","Full history vs only the last k steps."]],"minute":"An RNN reads a sequence one step at a time, updating a hidden state h_t = tanh(W_hh h_{t−1} + W_hx x_t + b) and predicting the next item with a softmax over W_ho h_t. The same weights are used at every step, so parameter count is independent of length: for d = 100, h = 256, V = 10,000 it is 2,661,392. Training maximises the sequence likelihood with backpropagation through time, summing gradients over steps. Repeated multiplication by the Jacobian makes gradients vanish (0.4²⁰ ≈ 10⁻⁸) or explode. GRUs (reset and update gates) and LSTMs (forget, input, output gates plus an additive cell state) keep information and gradients flowing. Bidirectional RNNs use both directions when the whole sequence is available; deep RNNs stack 2–4 layers. Applications include language modelling and time-series forecasting evaluated with MSE, RMSE and MAE."},"flashcards":[["Why not a feed-forward net for sequences?","Fixed input size, no memory, no parameter sharing across positions",5],["Autoregressive factorisation","$P(x_1..x_T)=\\prod_tP(x_t\\mid x_{<t})$",8],["k-th order Markov assumption","$P(x_t\\mid x_{<t})\\approx P(x_t\\mid x_{t-k..t-1})$",10],["Latent-variable update","$h_t=f(x_t,h_{t-1})$",12],["RNN hidden update","$h_t=\\phi(W_{hh}h_{t-1}+W_{hx}x_t+b_h)$",20],["Vanilla RNN parameters","$h(d+h+V+1)+V$; 2,661,392 for d=100, h=256, V=10k",24],["Slide forward pass h₁","(0.635, 0.462, 0.291)",26],["Perplexity","exp(average per-token cross-entropy)",31],["BPTT hidden gradient","local term + future term through $\\mathrm{diag}(1-h^2)W_{hh}$",34],["0.4^20","≈ 1.1 × 10⁻⁸: vanishing gradient",40],["Bidirectional output","$o_t=W_{ho}[\\overrightarrow h_t;\\overleftarrow h_t]+b_o$",45],["BiRNN parameters (h=128 each way)","2,628,624",48],["GRU final state","$h_t=z_t\\odot h_{t-1}+(1-z_t)\\odot\\tilde h_t$",66],["GRU parameters","$3(hd+h^2+h)+Vh+V$",72],["LSTM cell update","$c_t=f_t\\odot c_{t-1}+i_t\\odot\\tilde c_t$",80],["LSTM hidden output","$h_t=o_t\\odot\\tanh(c_t)$",81],["∂c_t/∂c_{t−1}","$f_t$ (gates fixed): additive path",84],["RMSE vs MAE","RMSE penalises large errors; MAE is robust and reads as average error",91]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["why","h1"],"deep":["r-motiv","r-ffail","r-dep"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2","h3"],"deep":["r-ar","r-arex","r-markov","r-markovex","r-latent","r-latentex","r-temp","r-temp2","r-temp3"],"viz":["tempForecast"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["what","h4","h5","h6","demo"],"deep":["r-rnn","r-unroll","r-math1","r-math2","r-share","r-params","r-paramex","r-fwd","r-act"],"viz":["rnnUnroll","rnnParams"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h7","h8"],"deep":["r-obj","r-loss","r-bptt","r-bpttgraph","r-bpttgrad","r-bpttex","r-bpttfwd","r-bpttback","r-bpttparam"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h9"],"deep":["r-vanish","r-vanishex","r-vanishwhy"],"viz":["vanishLab"],"s